  "risks": [
    "Machine orchestration, validation, DB writes, and UI state are tightly coupled in backend/controllers/machine_control.py",
    "Mixed global SQLAlchemy session and ad-hoc Session() usage across multiple threads",
    "No dedicated service/integration layer; controllers call data/hardware logic directly",
    "Critical state kept in-memory (_armed_code, _pending_starts, UI_STATE) with timers",
    "Asynchronous start confirmation via telemetry complicates external deduct sequencing",
    "Destructive admin delete endpoints in flask_server.py lack require_admin_auth decorators",
    "Stringly-typed settings storage with minimal validation for secrets/timeouts",
    "Startup performs seeding side effects automatically, reducing deployment determinism",
    "Error handling/retries for external service calls are not yet standardized",
    "Legacy local code model may conflict with external source-of-truth usage accounting"
  ],
